IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tla-dates`

-- Limitation Act 1974 (Tas) -- the rules a person bringing (or answering) a claim meets: Part I s 2 (date of
-- discoverability, disability); Part II Division 2 so far as it fixes the periods for personal injury, deaths, child
-- abuse, settled child abuse claims, contract, tort, statutory sums, deeds, judgments, interest and ship collisions
-- (ss 4, 5A, 5B, 5C, 8(2), (4), (7)); Division 3 for trusts and deceased estates (ss 24, 25); Division 4 for money paid as
-- a tax (ss 25C-25E); Part III (disability, the personal injury suspension, notices to proceed, acknowledgement and part
-- payment, fraud and mistake: ss 26, 26A, 27, 29-32); ss 35, 38 and 38A(3).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in tla-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "shall not",
-- "is not maintainable ... unless", "may not be granted", "cannot", "does not apply", a "while" or "if" condition that
-- fails); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The court's
-- judgments ("just and reasonable", "interests of justice", "thinks fit", "reasonable diligence", "ought to have known")
-- are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1974`

§§ `Days fixed by the Act`

-- s 38A(1): "amendment day means the day on which the amending Act commences" -- the Limitation Amendment Act 2017
-- (No. 52 of 2017), which the history notes show applied on 1 July 2018. Section 5B was inserted by the same Act on the
-- same day, so it is also "the day on which section 5B commenced" (s 5C(1)).
`the amendment day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2018

-- A day later than any real day, for a period with no end yet (a disability or suspension that has not ended).
`the far serial` MEANS 100000000

§§ `s 2(2), (3) -- disability`

-- s 2(2): "a person is deemed to be under disability while -- (a) he is an infant; (b) he is incapable, by reason of
-- mental disorder, of managing his property or affairs". s 2(3): conclusively presumed incapable "(a) while he or she is
-- subject to an assessment order or treatment order under the Mental Health Act 2013; or (b) while a guardianship order
-- or an administration order in respect of his estate is in force under the Guardianship and Administration Act 1995."
-- "Infant" is not defined in this Act: read as under 18 (finding 3). A "while" condition: JUST FALSE when no head holds.
GIVEN `I am an infant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am incapable by reason of mental disorder of managing my property or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am subject to an assessment order or treatment order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a guardianship or administration order for my estate is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) -- I am under a disability` `I am an infant` `I am incapable by reason of mental disorder of managing my property or affairs` `I am subject to an assessment order or treatment order` `a guardianship or administration order for my estate is in force` MEANS
    IF `I am an infant`
       OR `I am incapable by reason of mental disorder of managing my property or affairs`
       OR `I am subject to an assessment order or treatment order`
       OR `a guardianship or administration order for my estate is in force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5A(6) -- date of discoverability for a personal representative`

-- s 5A(6): for a plaintiff who is the personal representative of a deceased person, the date of discoverability is "the
-- earliest of the following times: (a) the date when the deceased person knew that personal injury -- (i) had occurred;
-- and (ii) was attributable to the conduct of the defendant; and (iii) was sufficiently significant to warrant bringing
-- proceedings; (b) the date when the personal representative was appointed, if he or she knew or ought to have known the
-- date of discoverability at that time; (c) the date when the personal representative first knew or ought to have known
-- the date of discoverability, if he or she acquired that knowledge or ought to have acquired that knowledge after being
-- appointed". (b) and (c) together give the later of the appointment and the representative's own knowledge; (a) asks
-- what the deceased actually knew, not what he or she ought to have known (finding 4).
GIVEN `the deceased knew all three things` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the deceased knew them` IS A DATE
      `the day I was appointed` IS A DATE
      `the day I first knew or ought to have known` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 5A(6) -- the date of discoverability for a personal representative` `the deceased knew all three things` `the day the deceased knew them` `the day I was appointed` `the day I first knew or ought to have known` MEANS
    IF `the deceased knew all three things`
    THEN `the earlier of` `the day the deceased knew them` `and` `the representative's day`
    ELSE `the representative's day`
    WHERE
        `the representative's day` MEANS `the later of` `the day I was appointed` `and` `the day I first knew or ought to have known`

§§ `s 5B -- no limitation period for the abuse of a minor`

-- s 5B(1): "Despite section 5A and section 26A -- (a) an action for damages for personal injury to a person arising from
-- or related to the sexual abuse, or serious physical abuse, of the person when the person was a minor; or (b) an action
-- for damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 in respect of the death of a person arising from or related to [that
-- abuse] -- may be brought at any time." (2): the abuse "includes any psychological abuse that arises from the sexual abuse
-- or the serious physical abuse". "Sexual abuse", "serious physical abuse" and "minor" are not defined: asked as facts.
DECLARE `Kind of abuse` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse`
    `other abuse or harm`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of abuse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is abuse section 5B or 5C names` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `other abuse or harm` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- A grant ("may be brought at any time") limited in its own wording: when the facts fall outside it the section is
-- silent and s 5A governs (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording; the case falls outside the limit).
GIVEN `it is a damages claim for personal injury or a Fatal Accidents Act claim for a death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the abuse was` IS A `Kind of abuse`
      `the person was a minor when abused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury or death arose from or related to the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B -- my action may be brought at any time` `it is a damages claim for personal injury or a Fatal Accidents Act claim for a death` `what the abuse was` `the person was a minor when abused` `the injury or death arose from or related to the abuse` MEANS
    IF `it is a damages claim for personal injury or a Fatal Accidents Act claim for a death`
       AND `it is abuse section 5B or 5C names` `what the abuse was`
       AND `the person was a minor when abused`
       AND `the injury or death arose from or related to the abuse`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 5C -- previously settled child abuse claims`

-- s 5C(1): "child abuse means -- (a) sexual abuse, or serious physical abuse, of a child; and (b) any psychological abuse
-- of the child that arises from [it] -- but does not include an act that is lawful at the time at which it occurs";
-- "previously settled relevant right of action means a relevant right of action that was settled before the day on which
-- section 5B commenced but after a limitation period applying before that day to the right of action had expired".
-- (2): "An action may be brought on a previously settled relevant right of action if a relevant court, by order on
-- application, sets aside the agreement effecting the settlement, on the grounds that it is in the interest of justice to
-- do so." (8): "This section does not apply in relation to an agreement effecting a settlement that is an offer of
-- redress accepted under section 42 of the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018".
DECLARE `Settlement outcome` IS ONE OF
    `section 5C does not apply to an accepted National Redress Scheme offer`
    `this is not a previously settled child abuse claim that section 5C reopens`
    `you may apply to the court to set the settlement aside, and may sue once it does`
    `the settlement has been set aside: you may bring the action`

GIVEN `what the abuse was` IS A `Kind of abuse`
      `I was a child when abused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was lawful when it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the settlement` IS A DATE
      `a limitation period had expired before the settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was an accepted National Redress Scheme offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has set the settlement aside in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Settlement outcome`
`s 5C -- what I can do about my earlier settlement` `what the abuse was` `I was a child when abused` `the act was lawful when it occurred` `the day of the settlement` `a limitation period had expired before the settlement` `it was an accepted National Redress Scheme offer` `the court has set the settlement aside in the interests of justice` MEANS
    IF `it was an accepted National Redress Scheme offer`
    THEN `section 5C does not apply to an accepted National Redress Scheme offer`
    ELSE IF `it is a previously settled relevant right of action`
         THEN IF `the court has set the settlement aside in the interests of justice`
              THEN `the settlement has been set aside: you may bring the action`
              ELSE `you may apply to the court to set the settlement aside, and may sue once it does`
         ELSE `this is not a previously settled child abuse claim that section 5C reopens`
    WHERE
        `it is a previously settled relevant right of action` MEANS
                `it is abuse section 5B or 5C names` `what the abuse was`
            AND `I was a child when abused`
            AND (NOT `the act was lawful when it occurred`)
            AND (`the day of the settlement` `is before` `the amendment day`)
            AND `a limitation period had expired before the settlement`

-- s 5C(6): the court "may, if it is satisfied that it is just and reasonable to do so when awarding damages ..., take into
-- account any amount, paid under an agreement that is wholly or partly void under subsection (4), to the extent to which
-- the amount relates to the child abuse". (7): "half of the total of all amounts paid under an agreement is taken to be
-- the amount relating to the child abuse ..., if the agreement -- (a) does not relate solely to the child abuse; and (b)
-- does not expressly indicate the extent to which the agreement and amounts paid under it relate to the child abuse."
-- The answer is the most the court may take into account; whether it does is its judgment.
GIVEN `the total paid under the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement related solely to the child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement expressly indicated the part for the child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part it indicated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 5C(6), (7) -- the most of my earlier payment the court may take into account` `the total paid under the agreement` `the agreement related solely to the child abuse` `the agreement expressly indicated the part for the child abuse` `the part it indicated` MEANS
    IF `the agreement related solely to the child abuse`
    THEN JUST `the total paid under the agreement`
    ELSE IF NOT `the agreement expressly indicated the part for the child abuse`
         THEN JUST (`the total paid under the agreement` DIVIDED BY 2)
         ELSE JUST `the part it indicated`

-- s 5C(5): "A party to an agreement that is wholly or partly void under subsection (4) cannot seek to recover an amount
-- paid by or in respect of the party under the agreement on the basis that the agreement is void to that extent." A flat
-- negative: JUST FALSE once the agreement has been set aside; before that, the section does not reach it (NOTHING-kind:
-- a prohibition limited in its own wording).
GIVEN `the court has set the agreement aside under s 5C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5C(5) -- the other party can recover what it paid me because the agreement is void` `the court has set the agreement aside under s 5C` MEANS
    IF `the court has set the agreement aside under s 5C`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 5A(5) and s 38A(3) -- the extension to 6 years`

-- s 5A(5): "A judge may extend the period of limitation referred to in subsection (3) to the expiration of 6 years
-- commencing on the date of discoverability if he or she considers that, in the circumstances of the case, it is just and
-- reasonable to do so." s 38A(3): "an extension ... may not be granted under section 5A(5) as in force after the amendment
-- day, in relation to a cause of action that accrued before that day, if the date of discoverability occurred more than 3
-- years before that day." More than 3 years before 1 July 2018 is any day before 1 July 2015 (fork F2). "May not be
-- granted": JUST FALSE; otherwise JUST TRUE (the judge may extend, if just and reasonable).
GIVEN `my cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my date of discoverability` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A(5) -- a judge may extend my period to 6 years` `my cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018` `my date of discoverability` MEANS
    IF `my cause of action accrued before 1 July 2018` AND (`my date of discoverability` `is before` (`the anniversary` (-3) `years after` `the amendment day`))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 26A(1), (2), (4) -- a relevant person`

-- s 26A(1): "capable parent, in relation to a minor, means a person -- (a) who is a parent of the minor; and (b) who is not
-- under a disability; and (c) who is not the intended defendant or a parent who is in a close relationship with the
-- intended defendant"; (2)(a): a parent is in a close relationship "if the parent, or another parent, may be directly or
-- indirectly influenced by the intended defendant not to bring an action". "legal representative ... means a person --
-- (a) who has legal authority to commence and conduct legal actions on behalf of the person ...; and (b) who is not the
-- intended defendant"; (2)(b): in a close relationship if the representative "may be directly or indirectly influenced by
-- the intended defendant not to bring an action".
-- (4): "A person is a relevant person -- (a) while the person is a minor and is not in the custody of a capable parent; or
-- (b) while the person is a person to whom section 2(2)(b) applies for a continuous period of 28 days or more and either --
-- (i) there is no legal representative in relation to the person; or (ii) the legal representative ... is in a close
-- relationship with the intended defendant." "While": JUST FALSE when neither head holds.
GIVEN `I am a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am in the custody of a parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that parent is under a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that parent is the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a parent may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have been incapable by mental disorder for a continuous 28 days or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have someone with legal authority to sue for me who is not the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that representative may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26A(4) -- I am a relevant person` `I am a minor` `I am in the custody of a parent` `that parent is under a disability` `that parent is the person I would sue` `a parent may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue` `I have been incapable by mental disorder for a continuous 28 days or more` `I have someone with legal authority to sue for me who is not the person I would sue` `that representative may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue` MEANS
    IF `head (a)` OR `head (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `in the custody of a capable parent` MEANS
                `I am in the custody of a parent`
            AND (NOT `that parent is under a disability`)
            AND (NOT `that parent is the person I would sue`)
            AND (NOT `a parent may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue`)
        `head (a)` MEANS `I am a minor` AND (NOT `in the custody of a capable parent`)
        `head (b)` MEANS
                `I have been incapable by mental disorder for a continuous 28 days or more`
            AND ((NOT `I have someone with legal authority to sue for me who is not the person I would sue`) OR `that representative may be influenced by the person I would sue not to sue`)

§§ `ss 29-31 -- acknowledgement and part payment`

-- s 29(4): "Where any right of action has accrued to recover any debt or other liquidated pecuniary claim, or any claim
-- to the personal estate of a deceased person or to any share or interest therein, and the person liable or accountable
-- therefor acknowledges the claim or makes any payment in respect thereof, the right shall be deemed to have accrued on
-- and not before the date of the acknowledgement or the last payment." s 30(1): an acknowledgement "shall be in writing
-- and signed by the person making the acknowledgement"; (2): it or a payment may be made by an agent, to the claimant or
-- an agent. s 31(5): an acknowledgement of a debt "shall bind the acknowledgor and his successors but not any other
-- person"; (7): a payment "shall bind all persons liable in respect thereof"; (8): a payment "made after the expiration of
-- the period of limitation ... shall not bind -- (a) any person other than the person making the payment and his
-- successors". Unlike some other Acts, s 29 has no "before the period expires": an acknowledgement or payment after expiry
-- revives the right against its maker (ss 31(6), (8), 39(1) assume so; finding 6).
DECLARE `Kind of acknowledgement` IS ONE OF
    `a written acknowledgement of my claim, signed by its maker`
    `a payment in respect of my claim`
    `an acknowledgement not in writing or not signed`
    `nothing of that kind`

DECLARE `Acknowledgement effect` IS ONE OF
    `my right is taken to accrue afresh on` HAS `the fresh accrual day` IS A DATE
    `it does not restart time against the person I would sue`
    `sections 29 to 31 do not restart time for this kind of claim`

GIVEN `my claim is for a debt or fixed sum, or to a deceased estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what was given` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement`
      `the day it was given` IS A DATE
      `the person I would sue made it, or their agent did` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made after my period had expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Acknowledgement effect`
`ss 29-31 -- the effect of the acknowledgement or payment` `my claim is for a debt or fixed sum, or to a deceased estate` `what was given` `the day it was given` `the person I would sue made it, or their agent did` `it was made after my period had expired` MEANS
    IF NOT `my claim is for a debt or fixed sum, or to a deceased estate`
    THEN `sections 29 to 31 do not restart time for this kind of claim`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what was given`
         WHEN `a written acknowledgement of my claim, signed by its maker` THEN
            IF `the person I would sue made it, or their agent did`
            THEN `my right is taken to accrue afresh on` `the day it was given`
            ELSE `it does not restart time against the person I would sue`
         WHEN `a payment in respect of my claim` THEN
            IF `the person I would sue made it, or their agent did` OR (NOT `it was made after my period had expired`)
            THEN `my right is taken to accrue afresh on` `the day it was given`
            ELSE `it does not restart time against the person I would sue`
         OTHERWISE `it does not restart time against the person I would sue`

§§ `s 25C -- recovering money paid as a tax`

-- s 25C(1): "An action is not maintainable against the Crown, an instrumentality of the Crown or a public authority to
-- recover money paid by way of a tax or purported tax or under a mistake unless the person bringing the action ...
-- satisfies the court -- (a) that the claimant has not charged to or recovered from, and will not charge to or recover
-- from, any other person any amount in respect of the whole or any part of the amount so paid; or (b) if the claimant has
-- so charged ..., that the claimant has reimbursed, or has contracted to reimburse, each other person for the amount
-- claimed in the action." "Not maintainable ... unless": JUST FALSE when neither holds. Whether the court is satisfied is
-- the court's; the facts are the claimant's.
GIVEN `I have passed on or will pass on any of the amount to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have reimbursed, or contracted to reimburse, each of them for the amount I claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25C -- my action to recover the tax is maintainable` `I have passed on or will pass on any of the amount to someone else` `I have reimbursed, or contracted to reimburse, each of them for the amount I claim` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I have passed on or will pass on any of the amount to someone else`) OR `I have reimbursed, or contracted to reimburse, each of them for the amount I claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 35 -- set-off and counterclaim`

-- s 35: "any claim by way of set-off or counterclaim shall be deemed to be a separate action and to have been commenced on
-- the same date as the action in which the set-off or counterclaim is pleaded."
GIVEN `the day the action against me was commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 35 -- the day my counterclaim is taken to be commenced` `the day the action against me was commenced` MEANS `the day the action against me was commenced`

§§ `What the time limit comes to`

DECLARE `Time limit` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period applies`
    `the last day to commence is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `time has not yet begun to count`
    `no last day yet, because the disability or suspension has not ended`
    `another Act's time limit applies`
    `not answered by this encoding`

§§ `Part III -- a spell that stops the clock (s 26A(3))`

-- One spell, as serial day numbers, first and last day inclusive. An absent spell has its first day after its last.
DECLARE `Spell` HAS
    `spell first serial` IS A NUMBER
    `spell last serial`  IS A NUMBER

`no spell` MEANS `Spell` WITH `spell first serial` IS `the far serial`, `spell last serial` IS 0

-- The last day (as a serial) after one spell: the days of the spell that fall on or after the start of the period, and
-- after any earlier spell already counted, are added, if the spell begins on or before the last day as it then stands
-- (s 26A(3): "suspended for each period in which the person is a relevant person"). A spell with no end yet, begun in
-- time, leaves no last day (fork F5).
GIVEN s IS A `Spell`, `the last so far` IS A NUMBER, `the period start` IS A NUMBER, `counted up to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last serial after` s `with last` `the last so far` `from` `the period start` `counted to` `counted up to` MEANS
    IF `the last so far` AT LEAST `the far serial`
    THEN `the last so far`
    ELSE IF (s's `spell last serial`) LESS THAN `the effective first`
         THEN `the last so far`
         ELSE IF `the effective first` GREATER THAN `the last so far`
              THEN `the last so far`
              ELSE IF (s's `spell last serial`) AT LEAST `the far serial`
                   THEN `the far serial`
                   ELSE `the last so far` PLUS ((s's `spell last serial`) MINUS `the effective first`) PLUS 1
    WHERE
        `the effective first` MEANS max (s's `spell first serial`) (max `the period start` (`counted up to` PLUS 1))

-- Two spells, taken in order of their first days.
GIVEN `spell one` IS A `Spell`, `spell two` IS A `Spell`, `the ordinary last` IS A NUMBER, `the period start` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last serial after spells` `spell one` `and` `spell two` `with last` `the ordinary last` `from` `the period start` MEANS
    `the last serial after` `the later spell` `with last` `after the earlier` `from` `the period start` `counted to` `the counted day`
    WHERE
        `the earlier spell` MEANS
            IF (`spell two`'s `spell first serial`) LESS THAN (`spell one`'s `spell first serial`)
            THEN `spell two`
            ELSE `spell one`
        `the later spell` MEANS
            IF (`spell two`'s `spell first serial`) LESS THAN (`spell one`'s `spell first serial`)
            THEN `spell one`
            ELSE `spell two`
        `after the earlier` MEANS `the last serial after` `the earlier spell` `with last` `the ordinary last` `from` `the period start` `counted to` (`the period start` MINUS 1)
        `the counted day` MEANS
            IF (`the earlier spell`'s `spell last serial`) LESS THAN (`the earlier spell`'s `spell first serial`)
            THEN `the period start` MINUS 1
            ELSE max (`the period start` MINUS 1) (`the earlier spell`'s `spell last serial`)

§§ `Personal injury and death claims (ss 5A, 5B, 26A, 32, 38, 38A)`

-- One action for damages for negligence, nuisance or breach of duty that include damages for personal injuries, or one
-- Fatal Accidents Act 1934 action for a death (s 5A(3), (4)); "breach of duty" read to include an intentional wrong
-- (fork F6).
DECLARE `The injury claim` HAS
    `injury: another Act sets the period`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: child abuse action under s 5B`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: discoverability day`               IS A DATE
    `injury: extension granted`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: accrued before 1 July 2018`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: birth day`                         IS A DATE
    `injury: minor spell`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: minor spell first day`             IS A DATE
    `injury: minor spell has ended`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: minor spell last day`              IS A DATE
    `injury: incapacity spell`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: incapacity spell first day`        IS A DATE
    `injury: incapacity spell has ended`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: incapacity spell last day`         IS A DATE
    `injury: fraud or mistake`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: fraud discovered`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: fraud discovery day`               IS A DATE

-- s 32(1): "the period of limitation shall not begin to run until the plaintiff has discovered the fraud or the mistake
-- ... or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it": the period starts on the later of the date of
-- discoverability and that day.
GIVEN c IS A `The injury claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`the injury period start` c MEANS
    IF c's `injury: fraud or mistake`
    THEN `the later of` (c's `injury: discoverability day`) `and` (c's `injury: fraud discovery day`)
    ELSE c's `injury: discoverability day`

-- s 5A(3): "must not be brought after the expiration of 3 years commencing on the date of discoverability"; (5): a judge
-- may extend it "to the expiration of 6 years commencing on the date of discoverability", unless s 38A(3) forbids it.
-- "Commencing on" the day: the day itself is the first day, so the last day is the day before the anniversary (fork F1).
GIVEN c IS A `The injury claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the injury period in years` c MEANS
    IF c's `injury: extension granted` AND (`s 5A(5) -- a judge may extend my period to 6 years` (c's `injury: accrued before 1 July 2018`) (c's `injury: discoverability day`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN 6
    ELSE 3

GIVEN c IS A `The injury claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`the injury ordinary last day` c MEANS `the last day of` (`the injury period in years` c) `years commencing on` (`the injury period start` c)

-- s 26A(3), (4)(a): the minor's spell ends at the latest on the day before the 18th birthday (fork F3).
GIVEN c IS A `The injury claim`
GIVETH A `Spell`
`the minor spell of` c MEANS
    IF c's `injury: minor spell`
    THEN `Spell` WITH `spell first serial` IS DATE_SERIAL (c's `injury: minor spell first day`), `spell last serial` IS min `the given last` (DATE_SERIAL (`the day of reaching age` 18 `for birth on` (c's `injury: birth day`)) MINUS 1)
    ELSE `no spell`
    WHERE
        `the given last` MEANS
            IF c's `injury: minor spell has ended`
            THEN DATE_SERIAL (c's `injury: minor spell last day`)
            ELSE `the far serial`

-- s 26A(4)(b): a spell of incapacity counts only if it lasts "a continuous period of 28 days or more" (one that has not
-- ended is counted: fork F5); the whole spell is suspended, not only the days after the 28th (fork F4).
GIVEN c IS A `The injury claim`
GIVETH A `Spell`
`the incapacity spell of` c MEANS
    IF c's `injury: incapacity spell` AND `long enough`
    THEN `Spell` WITH `spell first serial` IS DATE_SERIAL (c's `injury: incapacity spell first day`), `spell last serial` IS `the given last`
    ELSE `no spell`
    WHERE
        `the given last` MEANS
            IF c's `injury: incapacity spell has ended`
            THEN DATE_SERIAL (c's `injury: incapacity spell last day`)
            ELSE `the far serial`
        `long enough` MEANS
            IF c's `injury: incapacity spell has ended`
            THEN (`the given last` MINUS DATE_SERIAL (c's `injury: incapacity spell first day`)) PLUS 1 AT LEAST 28
            ELSE TRUE

GIVEN c IS A `The injury claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the injury last serial` c MEANS
    `the last serial after spells` (`the minor spell of` c) `and` (`the incapacity spell of` c) `with last` (DATE_SERIAL (`the injury ordinary last day` c)) `from` (DATE_SERIAL (`the injury period start` c))

-- s 38: "This Act does not apply to any action or arbitration for which a period of limitation is prescribed by any other
-- enactment." s 5B: "may be brought at any time", "despite section 5A and section 26A".
GIVEN c IS A `The injury claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the time limit for the injury claim` c MEANS
    IF c's `injury: another Act sets the period`
    THEN `another Act's time limit applies`
    ELSE IF c's `injury: child abuse action under s 5B`
         THEN `no limitation period applies`
         ELSE IF c's `injury: fraud or mistake` AND (NOT (c's `injury: fraud discovered`))
              THEN `time has not yet begun to count`
              ELSE IF `the injury last serial` c AT LEAST `the far serial`
                   THEN `no last day yet, because the disability or suspension has not ended`
                   ELSE `the last day to commence is` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (`the injury last serial` c))

§§ `Other claims (ss 4, 8, 24, 25, 25D, 25E, 26, 27, 29-32, 38)`

DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `a claim in contract or tort, other than for personal injury`
    `a claim for a sum recoverable under an enactment, other than a penalty`
    `a claim on a deed`
    `a claim on a judgment`
    `a claim for arrears of interest`
    `a claim to a deceased person's estate or a share in it`
    `a claim for arrears of interest on a legacy`
    `a beneficiary's claim against a trustee for fraud, or for trust property the trustee holds or converted`
    `a beneficiary's other claim for breach of trust or to recover trust property`
    `a claim against a ship or its owners for damage, loss or injury caused by another ship's fault`
    `a claim against the Crown or a public authority for money paid as a tax or under a mistake about a tax law`
    `another kind of claim`

-- The period, in years: s 4(1)(a), (d), 6 years; s 4(3), a specialty, 12 years; s 4(4), a judgment, 12 years from the date
-- it became enforceable; s 4(5), arrears of interest, 6 years after they became due; s 25, a claim to a deceased person's
-- personal estate or a share in it, 12 years from when the right to receive it accrued, and arrears of interest on a
-- legacy, 6 years from when the interest became due; s 24(2), a beneficiary's other action, 6 years; s 8(2), 2 years from
-- the day the damage, loss or injury was caused; s 25D(2), 12 months from payment (one year). s 24(1) and other kinds: 0
-- (not used).
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the period in years for` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a claim on a deed` THEN 12
    WHEN `a claim on a judgment` THEN 12
    WHEN `a claim to a deceased person's estate or a share in it` THEN 12
    WHEN `a claim against a ship or its owners for damage, loss or injury caused by another ship's fault` THEN 2
    WHEN `a claim against the Crown or a public authority for money paid as a tax or under a mistake about a tax law` THEN 1
    WHEN `a beneficiary's claim against a trustee for fraud, or for trust property the trustee holds or converted` THEN 0
    WHEN `another kind of claim` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 6

DECLARE `The claim` HAS
    `claim kind`                              IS A `Kind of claim`
    `another Act sets the period`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `accrual day`                             IS A DATE
    `claimant birth day`                      IS A DATE
    `incapable at accrual`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `incapacity has ended`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `incapacity end day`                      IS A DATE
    `first accrued to a predecessor not under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claimant has died`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `claimant death day`                      IS A DATE
    `notice to proceed served`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice to proceed day`                   IS A DATE
    `fraud or mistake`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud discovered`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud discovery day`                     IS A DATE
    `claim is for a debt or fixed sum`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `acknowledgement given`                   IS A `Kind of acknowledgement`
    `acknowledgement day`                     IS A DATE
    `acknowledged by the person I would sue`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `recoverable as an overpayment`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `court extended the ship claim period`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `ship claim extended to`                  IS A DATE

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`the claim period start` c MEANS
    IF c's `fraud or mistake`
    THEN `the later of` (c's `accrual day`) `and` (c's `fraud discovery day`)
    ELSE c's `accrual day`

-- s 26(1): "if on the date when any right of action accrued ... the person to whom it accrued was under a disability, the
-- action may be brought at any time before the expiration of 6 years, or in the case of any action for which a less
-- number of years is prescribed ... then such less number of years, from the date when the person ceased to be under a
-- disability or died whichever event first occurred notwithstanding that the period of limitation has expired." (2): not
-- where "the right of action first accrued to some person (not under a disability) through whom the person under a
-- disability claims". s 27(1): once a notice to proceed is served the person "shall ... be deemed to have ceased to be a
-- person under a disability". An infant ceases to be one on the 18th birthday (fork F3); a person under both heads ceases
-- when the later ends (fork F7). Answers the s 26 last day as a serial, the far serial while the disability lasts, or 0
-- where s 26 does not apply.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 26 last serial` c MEANS
    IF NOT `s 26 applies`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the day ceased` AT LEAST `the far serial`
         THEN `the far serial`
         ELSE DATE_SERIAL (`the anniversary` (min 6 (`the period in years for` (c's `claim kind`))) `years after` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL `the day ceased`))
    WHERE
        `the 18th birthday` MEANS `the day of reaching age` 18 `for birth on` (c's `claimant birth day`)
        `an infant at accrual` MEANS (c's `accrual day`) `is before` `the 18th birthday`
        `s 26 applies` MEANS (`an infant at accrual` OR c's `incapable at accrual`) AND (NOT (c's `first accrued to a predecessor not under disability`))
        `infancy end` MEANS
            IF `an infant at accrual`
            THEN DATE_SERIAL `the 18th birthday`
            ELSE 0
        `incapacity end` MEANS
            IF NOT (c's `incapable at accrual`)
            THEN 0
            ELSE IF c's `incapacity has ended`
                 THEN DATE_SERIAL (c's `incapacity end day`)
                 ELSE `the far serial`
        `death end` MEANS
            IF c's `claimant has died`
            THEN DATE_SERIAL (c's `claimant death day`)
            ELSE `the far serial`
        `notice end` MEANS
            IF c's `notice to proceed served`
            THEN DATE_SERIAL (c's `notice to proceed day`)
            ELSE `the far serial`
        `the day ceased` MEANS min (min (max `infancy end` `incapacity end`) `death end`) `notice end`

-- The last day under Part II with s 26 and s 32, before any acknowledgement or payment.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last serial before acknowledgement` c MEANS
    max (DATE_SERIAL (`the anniversary` (`the period in years for` (c's `claim kind`)) `years after` (`the claim period start` c))) (`the s 26 last serial` c)

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is for a debt, a fixed sum or a deceased estate` c IF
    c's `claim is for a debt or fixed sum` OR (c's `claim kind` EQUALS `a claim to a deceased person's estate or a share in it`)

-- The general case, with ss 26, 27, 29-32.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the general time limit for` c MEANS
    IF c's `fraud or mistake` AND (NOT (c's `fraud discovered`))
    THEN `time has not yet begun to count`
    ELSE IF `the last serial before acknowledgement` c AT LEAST `the far serial`
         THEN `no last day yet, because the disability or suspension has not ended`
         ELSE CONSIDER `ss 29-31 -- the effect of the acknowledgement or payment` (`the claim is for a debt, a fixed sum or a deceased estate` c) (c's `acknowledgement given`) (c's `acknowledgement day`) (c's `acknowledged by the person I would sue`) (DATE_SERIAL (c's `acknowledgement day`) GREATER THAN `the last serial before acknowledgement` c)
              WHEN `my right is taken to accrue afresh on` `the fresh day` THEN
                  `the last day to commence is` (`the later of` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (`the last serial before acknowledgement` c)) `and` (`the anniversary` (`the period in years for` (c's `claim kind`)) `years after` `the fresh day`))
              OTHERWISE `the last day to commence is` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (`the last serial before acknowledgement` c))

-- The whole answer. s 38: another enactment's period displaces this Act. s 24(1): "No period of limitation prescribed by
-- this Act shall apply" to a beneficiary's action for the trustee's fraud or to recover trust property the trustee holds
-- or converted. s 25D(2): a tax paid after the 1993 amendment, 12 months from payment; s 25D(3): not where the amount is
-- recoverable as an overpayment (NOTHING-kind: the text points to the taxing Act); s 25E: "cannot be extended", so no
-- Part III. s 8(2): 2 years; (4): the court may extend it; (7): "Part III does not apply". Other kinds: not answered.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the time limit for` c MEANS
    IF c's `another Act sets the period`
    THEN `another Act's time limit applies`
    ELSE CONSIDER c's `claim kind`
         WHEN `a beneficiary's claim against a trustee for fraud, or for trust property the trustee holds or converted` THEN `no limitation period applies`
         WHEN `another kind of claim` THEN `not answered by this encoding`
         WHEN `a claim against the Crown or a public authority for money paid as a tax or under a mistake about a tax law` THEN
             IF c's `recoverable as an overpayment`
             THEN `not answered by this encoding`
             ELSE `the last day to commence is` (`the anniversary` 1 `years after` (c's `accrual day`))
         WHEN `a claim against a ship or its owners for damage, loss or injury caused by another ship's fault` THEN
             IF c's `court extended the ship claim period`
             THEN `the last day to commence is` (`the later of` `the two year day` `and` (c's `ship claim extended to`))
             ELSE `the last day to commence is` `the two year day`
         OTHERWISE `the general time limit for` c
    WHERE
        `the two year day` MEANS `the anniversary` 2 `years after` (c's `accrual day`)

§§ `The time bar as a regulative rule`

-- "shall not be brought after the expiration of" the period: what the plaintiff must do to keep the action. The rule
-- starts on a day and allows the days to the last day; FULFILLED means in time and anything else too late. It takes a
-- DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `commence the action`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the action must be commenced within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the plaintiff`
    MUST `commence the action`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "the limitation period has expired: the action shall not be brought unless a judge extends the time where the Act allows (s 5A(5), s 8(4))"

GIVEN `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commencing at` `the time of the step` `satisfies` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the plaintiff` `commence the action` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether an action commenced on a day is in time under a time limit. JUST FALSE once the period has run ("shall not be
-- brought after"); JUST TRUE where no period applies, none has begun to run or none has yet been fixed; NOTHING under
-- another Act or outside the encoding (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text).
GIVEN `the day of commencing` IS A DATE, `the limit` IS A `Time limit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an action commenced on` `the day of commencing` `is in time under` `the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `no limitation period applies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `time has not yet begun to count` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `no last day yet, because the disability or suspension has not ended` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the last day to commence is` `the final day` THEN
        IF `commencing at` (`the days from` `the base` `to` `the day of commencing`) `satisfies` (`the action must be commenced within` (`the days from` `the base` `to` `the final day`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
        WHERE
            `the base` MEANS `the earlier of` `the day of commencing` `and` `the final day`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
